1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,000
-This is my little brother, George.
-[snorts]

3
00:00:08,066 --> 00:00:10,299
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:12,000
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,066 --> 00:00:14,100
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:17,566 --> 00:00:19,200
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:19,266 --> 00:00:22,500
[narrator] Peppa and her friends
are playing at Rebecca Rabbit's house.

9
00:00:22,566 --> 00:00:24,033
[all giggling]

10
00:00:24,099 --> 00:00:26,599
[woofs] Let's play hide-and-seek.

11
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:30,366
[bleats] We'll all hide,
and Peppa can find us.

12
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:33,433
Okay. One, two...

13
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,366
[narrator] Everyone must find
a hiding place before Peppa counts to ten.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,466
Danny and Candy are hiding
in the branches of a little tree.

15
00:00:41,533 --> 00:00:45,699
Zoë, Pedro and Rebecca are hiding
behind a fence.

16
00:00:45,766 --> 00:00:49,300
Suzy and Emily are hiding behind a bush.

17
00:00:49,366 --> 00:00:54,233
...nine, ten!
Ready or not, here I come!

18
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,633
[giggles] I know where you are.

19
00:00:57,199 --> 00:00:58,066
Oh!

20
00:00:58,133 --> 00:00:59,666
[giggling]

21
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:00,599
Oh.

22
00:01:00,666 --> 00:01:03,000
[narrator] Peppa cannot find anyone.

23
00:01:03,066 --> 00:01:05,800
[sighs] This is impossible.

24
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:06,733
[bell dings]

25
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,633
[narrator] Freddy Fox has come to play.

26
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,233
[snorts] Hello, Freddy.

27
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:13,300
[barks] Hello, Peppa. What are you doing?

28
00:01:13,366 --> 00:01:17,800
We're playing hide-and-seek.
But I can't find anyone.

29
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:20,233
Shall I find them for you?

30
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,433
You can try, but it's impossible.

31
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,633
[barks] Watch this.

32
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,466
[Freddy sniffing]

33
00:01:28,366 --> 00:01:31,266
-Found you.
-[all] Oh! Hello, Freddy.

34
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,566
-Aha! There you are!
-[both] Oh.

35
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,699
-Boo!
-[both] Oh!

36
00:01:36,766 --> 00:01:39,233
[narrator] Freddy Fox has found everyone.

37
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,333
How did you do that?

38
00:01:41,399 --> 00:01:43,633
I'm good at smelling.

39
00:01:43,699 --> 00:01:46,166
What's smelling got to do with it?

40
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:50,399
I can find you by sniffing your smell.

41
00:01:50,466 --> 00:01:55,366
[bleats] I'm not smelly.
I had a bath last night.

42
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:58,600
I know. You smell nice.

43
00:01:58,666 --> 00:02:00,033
Oh. [giggles]

44
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:04,233
[barks] I could even find you
with my eyes closed.

45
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:08,666
Go on, then. [snorts]
Find Suzy with your eyes closed.

46
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,066
Easy.

47
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,666
Hide, Suzy.

48
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:15,266
[all] One, two, three, four...

49
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:17,600
[narrator] Suzy is looking
for somewhere to hide.

50
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:22,733
...six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

51
00:02:22,799 --> 00:02:26,633
Ready or not, here I come. [sniffing]

52
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:30,166
[narrator] Freddy is looking for Suzy
with his eyes closed.

53
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:32,766
He is sniffing
where Suzy Sheep has walked:

54
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,233
round the tree...

55
00:02:34,299 --> 00:02:35,799
behind the little bush...

56
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:38,466
and back up the hill.

57
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:41,433
-Found you!
-[Suzy] Oh! [giggles]

58
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,700
All thanks to my nose.

59
00:02:44,766 --> 00:02:46,500
It's a super nose!

60
00:02:46,566 --> 00:02:48,299
Yes, it is.

61
00:02:48,366 --> 00:02:51,200
Has everything got a smell?

62
00:02:51,266 --> 00:02:55,700
Oh, yes. Everything has a different smell.

63
00:02:55,766 --> 00:02:57,500
What do I smell of?

64
00:02:57,566 --> 00:02:58,433
[Freddy sniffs]

65
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:03,000
You smell of flowers and Wellington boots.

66
00:03:03,066 --> 00:03:04,266
[all laugh]

67
00:03:04,333 --> 00:03:06,133
What do I smell of?

68
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:11,133
[sniffs] You smell of wet grass
and biscuits.

69
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,533
[all laugh]

70
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,266
What do I smell of?

71
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:18,200
-[sniffs] Bananas and jam.
-[laughs]

72
00:03:18,266 --> 00:03:19,700
What do I smell of?

73
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:24,233
-[sniffs] Milk and fish fingers.
-[laughs]

74
00:03:24,299 --> 00:03:26,000
What do I smell of?

75
00:03:26,066 --> 00:03:30,333
[sniffs] Pedro, you smell of toothpaste.

76
00:03:30,399 --> 00:03:31,266
Oh.

77
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,600
What's your favorite smell?

78
00:03:33,666 --> 00:03:34,700
Eggs.

79
00:03:34,766 --> 00:03:37,500
What is the worst thing
you've ever smelled?

80
00:03:37,566 --> 00:03:40,000
Blue cheese.

81
00:03:40,066 --> 00:03:42,100
[all] Pooey! [laugh]

82
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:43,033
[sniffs]

83
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,133
It's nearly dinnertime.

84
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,533
How do you know?

85
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,666
I can smell carrot soup.

86
00:03:49,733 --> 00:03:50,799
[all sniff]

87
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:53,666
I can smell carrot soup, too.

88
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,133
[all] And me!

89
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:58,733
Dinner's ready!
Come and get your carrot soup.

90
00:03:58,799 --> 00:04:00,399
[all giggling]

91
00:04:00,466 --> 00:04:04,333
[narrator] Everyone is enjoying
Mommy Rabbit's carrot soup.

92
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
This soup is yummy.

93
00:04:07,066 --> 00:04:09,066
-[horn honks outside]
-Who can that be?

94
00:04:09,533 --> 00:04:12,100
[narrator] Mr. Fox has come
to take Freddy home.

95
00:04:12,166 --> 00:04:14,033
[sniffs] Mm.

96
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:15,666
I can smell dinner.

97
00:04:15,733 --> 00:04:18,066
Oh, Mr. Fox. Hello.

98
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,399
Hello, Mommy Rabbit.

99
00:04:19,466 --> 00:04:24,266
Hello, Dad. I've just had my dinner
down a rabbit hole.

100
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:25,233
Good lad.

101
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,466
And can you guess what's for pudding?

102
00:04:27,533 --> 00:04:32,466
[sniffs] Smells nice. [sniffs]
I'd say strawberry jelly.

103
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:33,800
That's right!

104
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:36,800
[narrator] Mr. Fox loves smelling things.

105
00:04:37,033 --> 00:04:38,099
[all sniff]

106
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:39,400
[children] Mm.

107
00:04:39,466 --> 00:04:41,700
[narrator] Everyone loves smelling things.

108
00:04:41,766 --> 00:04:43,766
[all laughing]

109
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,266
[whistling]

110
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:50,633
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

111
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:56,666
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny morning,
and Daddy Pig is reading his newspaper.

112
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:57,733
[Daddy Pig whistling]

113
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,666
Daddy, what are you doing?

114
00:04:59,733 --> 00:05:01,633
I'm reading the newspaper.

115
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,099
[Daddy Pig whistling]

116
00:05:03,166 --> 00:05:05,633
You're making a funny sound.

117
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:08,166
-I'm whistling.
-Oh.

118
00:05:08,233 --> 00:05:10,633
Whistling is fun. You should try it.

119
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,200
I don't know how to.

120
00:05:12,266 --> 00:05:15,766
It's easy.
Just put your lips together and blow.

121
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,300
[Daddy pig whistles]

122
00:05:17,366 --> 00:05:18,300
[blows air]

123
00:05:18,366 --> 00:05:20,700
Try making a smaller O shape.

124
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:22,466
[Peppa blows raspberry]

125
00:05:22,533 --> 00:05:24,266
[both laugh]

126
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:26,433
Like this. [whistles]

127
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,133
And then you can whistle a tune.

128
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,200
[whistling upbeat tune]

129
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:34,433
[Peppa blowing air]

130
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:38,533
[sighs] I've got the wrong kind of mouth.

131
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:41,700
Your mouth is fine.
You just need to practice.

132
00:05:42,333 --> 00:05:43,266
[blows air]

133
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:45,066
It's impossible.

134
00:05:45,133 --> 00:05:48,433
It takes time to learn
how to do important things,

135
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:51,800
like riding a bicycle
or playing the piano.

136
00:05:52,033 --> 00:05:55,333
[snorts] It took me years
to learn how to wiggle my ears.

137
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,000
Wow! [giggles]

138
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:04,400
[narrator] Mommy Pig is in the kitchen
making cookies.

139
00:06:05,366 --> 00:06:07,099
[blowing air]

140
00:06:07,166 --> 00:06:08,733
What are you doing, Peppa?

141
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,633
I'm learning to whistle.

142
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,133
Oh, I see.

143
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,099
[Peppa blows air]

144
00:06:13,166 --> 00:06:15,000
Mommy, can you whistle?

145
00:06:15,066 --> 00:06:17,099
I don't know. I've never tried.

146
00:06:17,166 --> 00:06:19,333
It takes a lot of practice.

147
00:06:20,166 --> 00:06:22,000
[whistles]

148
00:06:22,066 --> 00:06:22,766
Oh, yes.

149
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,233
[narrator] Mommy Pig can whistle.

150
00:06:25,299 --> 00:06:28,400
You can whistle
because you are old, Mommy.

151
00:06:28,466 --> 00:06:30,000
Thank you, Peppa.

152
00:06:30,733 --> 00:06:32,066
[Peppa blowing air]

153
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:37,099
Vrrroom!

154
00:06:37,166 --> 00:06:40,433
[narrator] George is in the bedroom
playing with his toy rocket.

155
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,033
Vrrroom!

156
00:06:42,099 --> 00:06:45,033
George, I'm learning to whistle.

157
00:06:45,099 --> 00:06:49,266
You make an O shape with your mouth
and blow.

158
00:06:50,733 --> 00:06:52,500
Don't worry, George.

159
00:06:52,566 --> 00:06:57,266
It's almost impossible,
like wiggling your ears.

160
00:06:58,366 --> 00:07:00,166
[narrator] George can wiggle his ears.

161
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:01,633
[giggling]

162
00:07:02,433 --> 00:07:04,266
[snorts] Whistling is harder.

163
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:05,666
[whistles]

164
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:07,233
[narrator] George can whistle.

165
00:07:07,299 --> 00:07:08,166
Oh.

166
00:07:08,233 --> 00:07:09,533
[George whistles]

167
00:07:09,599 --> 00:07:11,033
[giggles]

168
00:07:16,166 --> 00:07:18,266
-[sighs]
-What's wrong, Peppa?

169
00:07:18,333 --> 00:07:22,133
[snorts] I can't whistle,
but everybody else can.

170
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:26,233
Never mind. I'm making cookies.
Would you like to lick the spoon?

171
00:07:26,299 --> 00:07:31,299
No, thank you, Mommy.
[snorts] Can I ring Suzy Sheep instead?

172
00:07:31,366 --> 00:07:32,400
Okay, Peppa.

173
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,166
[rings]

174
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,200
[bleats] Hello, Mrs. Pig.

175
00:07:38,266 --> 00:07:41,333
Hello, Mrs. Sheep.
Can Peppa talk to Suzy, please?

176
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,299
Hello, Suzy.

177
00:07:43,366 --> 00:07:46,633
[bleats] Hello, Peppa. What are you doing?

178
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:50,266
I'm learning to whistle,
but I can't do it yet.

179
00:07:50,333 --> 00:07:52,766
Hmm. That sounds hard.

180
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,066
It's impossible.
Uh, can you whistle, Suzy?

181
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:58,133
No.

182
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:02,799
[snorts] Oh, good. I mean,
that's sad if you can't whistle,

183
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:05,266
but good because I can't whistle.

184
00:08:05,733 --> 00:08:07,700
What's whistling, anyway?

185
00:08:07,766 --> 00:08:10,433
You put your lips together and blow.

186
00:08:11,066 --> 00:08:12,233
Like this?

187
00:08:12,299 --> 00:08:13,500
[whistles]

188
00:08:14,166 --> 00:08:15,566
[dial tone humming]

189
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:17,299
Hello? Peppa?

190
00:08:19,099 --> 00:08:20,466
The cookies are ready!

191
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:22,633
-Oh, goody. Cookies!
-[George snorts]

192
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:25,266
They'll be hot.
You should blow on them first.

193
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:26,799
Ooh, ah. [blows air]

194
00:08:27,033 --> 00:08:28,366
[giggles, then blows air]

195
00:08:28,433 --> 00:08:32,266
-Do you not want a cookie, Peppa?
-No, thank you, Mommy.

196
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:36,500
I think I might go outside
and be on my own for a little bit.

197
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,666
[snorts] Can you whistle yet?

198
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:47,800
It's no use, Daddy.
I'm never going to whistle, ever.

199
00:08:48,033 --> 00:08:49,466
Have you been practicing?

200
00:08:49,533 --> 00:08:53,600
[snorts] Yes, lots. But it doesn't work.

201
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:57,333
You need a little rest, Peppa.
Here, have a cookie.

202
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,333
It's hot. You should blow.

203
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,133
[whistles]

204
00:09:01,199 --> 00:09:02,633
Oh, what's that?

205
00:09:02,699 --> 00:09:05,533
It sounded like a whistle to me.

206
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,600
[Peppa whistling upbeat tune]

207
00:09:08,166 --> 00:09:10,166
-[Peppa giggles]
-What a lovely tune.

208
00:09:10,233 --> 00:09:12,233
[narrator] Peppa has learned
how to whistle.

209
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,266
[giggles] I can whistle!

210
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:16,333
[all whistling upbeat tune]

211
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,100
[bell ringing]

212
00:09:19,166 --> 00:09:21,166
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

213
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:23,533
[narrator] It is a school day.

214
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:28,166
Children, Dr. Hamster has come
to talk to us today.

215
00:09:28,233 --> 00:09:29,666
Hello, everyone.

216
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:31,733
[all] Hello, Dr. Hamster.

217
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:34,666
Dr. Hamster is a vet.

218
00:09:34,733 --> 00:09:37,166
Who knows what a vet does?

219
00:09:37,233 --> 00:09:40,666
[bleats] Vets help sick pets get better.

220
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:45,633
That's right. And I've brought
some of my pets to show you.

221
00:09:45,699 --> 00:09:46,566
[all] Ooh.

222
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:49,166
This is Binkie the budgie.

223
00:09:49,233 --> 00:09:50,699
[all] Hello, Binkie.

224
00:09:50,766 --> 00:09:53,000
[woofs] Can I stroke Binkie?

225
00:09:53,066 --> 00:09:55,166
Yes, very gently.

226
00:09:55,699 --> 00:09:57,100
He feels fluffy.

227
00:09:57,166 --> 00:10:01,466
Those are his feathers.
They help him to fly.

228
00:10:02,633 --> 00:10:03,500
[students giggle]

229
00:10:03,566 --> 00:10:07,433
[Dr. Hamster] Flying is how Binkie
gets his exercise.

230
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:13,000
Can you tell me what else Binkie needs
to stay fit and healthy?

231
00:10:13,066 --> 00:10:16,533
-[snorts] He needs to eat.
-Yes.

232
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:19,199
-He needs to drink.
-That's right.

233
00:10:19,266 --> 00:10:23,233
-He needs to breathe a bit.
-Very good.

234
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:26,199
-He needs to sleep.
-Excellent.

235
00:10:26,266 --> 00:10:30,366
[yawns] Sorry, Madame Gazelle.
I overslept.

236
00:10:30,433 --> 00:10:33,600
Oh, Pedro, you do like sleeping.

237
00:10:33,666 --> 00:10:36,133
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

238
00:10:36,199 --> 00:10:39,233
I have got a pet here who loves sleeping.

239
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,033
It's a tortoise.

240
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,500
It's Tiddles the tortoise.

241
00:10:43,566 --> 00:10:45,066
[students] Hello, Tiddles.

242
00:10:45,133 --> 00:10:49,166
Tiddles has slept all through the winter.

243
00:10:49,233 --> 00:10:50,166
[students] Ooh.

244
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:53,333
Why has he got that shell thing
on his back?

245
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:59,000
That shell is his house.
It's where he hides if he gets scared.

246
00:10:59,066 --> 00:11:01,199
Would you like to stroke him?

247
00:11:01,266 --> 00:11:02,633
Yes, please.

248
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:05,366
Don't be scared, Tiddles.

249
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:08,233
How old is he?

250
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:11,166
Tiddles is 33.

251
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:12,800
That's as old as my mom.

252
00:11:13,033 --> 00:11:17,600
But tortoises can live
for a hundred years.

253
00:11:17,666 --> 00:11:20,433
[snorts] That's as old as my grandpa.

254
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,366
Why is he so slow?

255
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:25,466
He has to carry his house on his back.

256
00:11:26,033 --> 00:11:31,166
Uh, Dr. Hamster,
I think Tiddles is escaping.

257
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:33,233
He can't go far.

258
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,433
Because he is so slow.

259
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,500
I've got someone else to show you here.

260
00:11:39,566 --> 00:11:41,066
[snorts] Dinosaur.

261
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:46,033
Oh, George. You always say dinosaur.

262
00:11:46,566 --> 00:11:49,333
Oh, it is a dinosaur.

263
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,600
[students] Ooh.

264
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:55,666
She's not a dinosaur.
This is Lulu the lizard.

265
00:11:55,733 --> 00:11:57,400
[students] Hello, Lulu.

266
00:11:58,033 --> 00:12:00,766
She's scaley like a dragon.

267
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,666
Can she breathe fire?

268
00:12:02,733 --> 00:12:07,633
No, but she has a very long tongue.

269
00:12:07,699 --> 00:12:09,199
[students] Wow!

270
00:12:09,266 --> 00:12:12,800
Does she sleep through the winter
like Tiddles?

271
00:12:13,033 --> 00:12:16,233
No. Oh, where is Tiddles?

272
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,233
Tiddles?

273
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:21,633
[narrator] Oh, dear.
Tiddles the tortoise has run away.

274
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:25,333
Don't worry, Dr. Hamster,
we'll find Tiddles.

275
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,733
Is he in the music room?

276
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:30,333
[narrator] Tiddles is not
in the music room.

277
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,233
Is he in the playhouse?

278
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:35,166
[narrator] Tiddles is not
in the playhouse.

279
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:37,633
Is he hiding by the coats?

280
00:12:37,699 --> 00:12:40,333
[narrator] Tiddles is not hiding
by the coats.

281
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,466
[sniffs]

282
00:12:41,533 --> 00:12:45,533
I can smell Tiddles. This way. [sniffing]

283
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:48,633
[narrator] Freddy Fox has
a very good sense of smell.

284
00:12:49,233 --> 00:12:51,333
There's Tiddles!

285
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,300
[narrator] Tiddles is up a tree.

286
00:12:53,366 --> 00:12:55,333
Oh, I'd better call for help.

287
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,133
[narrator] This is
Miss Rabbit's Fire Station.

288
00:12:59,166 --> 00:13:01,733
[screams] Fire! Fire!

289
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,233
Fire station. Where's the fire?

290
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:07,000
My Tiddles is up a tree.

291
00:13:07,066 --> 00:13:08,333
[Miss Rabbit] What? Again?

292
00:13:10,033 --> 00:13:14,566
Emergency! Emergency!
Tortoise up a tree!

293
00:13:15,133 --> 00:13:19,133
I don't know why
you like climbing trees so much.

294
00:13:19,199 --> 00:13:20,800
You're a tortoise.

295
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:23,033
[siren wailing]

296
00:13:23,099 --> 00:13:24,300
Stand back.

297
00:13:24,766 --> 00:13:26,733
Tiddles. [clicks tongue]

298
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,133
Come on, Tiddles.

299
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:29,533
[students] Hooray!

300
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:31,433
Thank you, Miss Rabbit.

301
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,466
Just doing my job.

302
00:13:33,533 --> 00:13:36,599
And my job is looking after pets.

303
00:13:36,666 --> 00:13:39,133
Where are Binkie and Lulu?

304
00:13:39,199 --> 00:13:40,566
Oh, I don't know.

305
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:44,566
Ah-ho. Here they are. Safe and sound.

306
00:13:44,633 --> 00:13:46,633
[all laughing]

307
00:13:50,066 --> 00:13:52,300
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

308
00:13:52,366 --> 00:13:54,699
[narrator] It is bedtime
for Peppa and George.

309
00:13:54,766 --> 00:13:59,766
Tomorrow we're going on a coach trip
to the seaside.

310
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,666
[snorts] We can make sand castles.

311
00:14:02,733 --> 00:14:05,300
-I fancy a swim.
-Me, too.

312
00:14:05,366 --> 00:14:08,400
The weather forecast says
it's going to be sunny.

313
00:14:08,466 --> 00:14:10,733
Good night, Peppa. Good night, George.

314
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:16,199
[narrator] Oh, it is starting to snow.

315
00:14:17,133 --> 00:14:18,433
[rooster crows]

316
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,533
[narrator] It is morning.

317
00:14:20,599 --> 00:14:23,000
Yippee! It's sunny!

318
00:14:23,599 --> 00:14:25,633
[gasps] Snow!

319
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:28,566
[narrator] A lot of snow has fallen
in the night.

320
00:14:29,199 --> 00:14:33,166
Snow, Mommy. Snow, Daddy.
Snow, snow, snow!

321
00:14:33,233 --> 00:14:34,800
-[George giggles]
-Eh? What?

322
00:14:35,433 --> 00:14:38,533
We are still going to the seaside,
aren't we?

323
00:14:38,599 --> 00:14:42,033
Well, let's see how much snow there is.

324
00:14:43,366 --> 00:14:45,633
Oh, where's Daddy gone?

325
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:50,033
[gasps] It's a walking snowman!

326
00:14:50,099 --> 00:14:51,733
[Daddy Pig in muffled voice] I'm cold.

327
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,766
[giggles] It's a walking, talking snowman!

328
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,166
[Daddy Pig shivers]

329
00:14:56,233 --> 00:14:58,766
Oh, it's just Daddy.

330
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,033
Poor Daddy. Let's warm you up.

331
00:15:01,099 --> 00:15:01,800
[all laughing]

332
00:15:02,033 --> 00:15:05,466
[narrator] Mommy Pig, Peppa and George
are warming Daddy Pig up

333
00:15:05,533 --> 00:15:07,266
by rubbing him with towels.

334
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:08,466
That's better.

335
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:11,233
[snorts] Now we can go to the seaside.

336
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,733
But what about the snow?

337
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:15,300
I don't think
the coach will be running today.

338
00:15:15,366 --> 00:15:16,266
Oh.

339
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:17,366
[bell dings]

340
00:15:17,433 --> 00:15:20,300
[narrator] Miss Rabbit's coach has arrived
at Peppa's house.

341
00:15:20,366 --> 00:15:24,566
[snorts] Goodness me.
How did you get through all that snow?

342
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:26,699
With my big snowplow.

343
00:15:26,766 --> 00:15:29,533
[narrator] Snowplows push the snow
out of the way.

344
00:15:29,599 --> 00:15:31,099
Hello, everyone.

345
00:15:31,166 --> 00:15:32,566
[children] Hello, Peppa.

346
00:15:32,633 --> 00:15:36,066
[narrator] All of Peppa's friends
are going to the seaside, too.

347
00:15:36,133 --> 00:15:37,000
[bell dings]

348
00:15:37,066 --> 00:15:39,166
Next stop, the seaside.

349
00:15:39,233 --> 00:15:40,666
[passengers] Hooray!

350
00:15:41,699 --> 00:15:45,000
[narrator] Mr. Bull and his friends
are gritting the road.

351
00:15:45,066 --> 00:15:47,166
The grit melts the snow.

352
00:15:47,233 --> 00:15:48,633
Hello, Mr. Bull.

353
00:15:48,699 --> 00:15:53,666
[moos] Hello, Miss Rabbit.
It's taken us all night,

354
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:58,033
but the road is clear
all the way to seaside.

355
00:15:58,099 --> 00:16:02,533
That's good. We're going to the seaside.
Would you like to come along?

356
00:16:02,599 --> 00:16:07,400
No, thanks, Miss Rabbit. [sniffs]
We've got more roads to grit.

357
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:13,099
-[passengers] Goodbye, Mr. Bull.
-Bye! Have a lovely day at the beach.

358
00:16:13,566 --> 00:16:17,199
♪ We're all going on a seaside holiday ♪

359
00:16:17,266 --> 00:16:20,666
♪ Sand castles, swimming and sunny skies ♪

360
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:24,500
♪ We're all going on a seaside holiday ♪

361
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:27,766
♪ Sea and sand and ice cream, too ♪

362
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,400
-[passengers laugh]
-[bell dings]

363
00:16:29,466 --> 00:16:32,133
Here we are, the seaside!

364
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:34,733
[narrator] The beach is covered in snow.

365
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,300
-[all] Oh!
-That sea looks cold.

366
00:16:37,366 --> 00:16:43,066
-I was looking forward to having a swim.
-You still can. The sea's not frozen over.

367
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:46,166
Come along, girls.
What are you waiting for?

368
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:51,099
Um... I can't swim,
because I've sprained my ankle.

369
00:16:51,166 --> 00:16:54,033
And I think I might have a cough. [coughs]

370
00:16:54,099 --> 00:16:57,099
Come on in, Mommy Pig. It's lovely.

371
00:16:57,166 --> 00:16:59,233
Are you sure it's lovely?

372
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:03,300
-Of course. The sea is wonderful today.
-Okay, then.

373
00:17:03,366 --> 00:17:05,733
[narrator] Mommy Pig is going for a swim.

374
00:17:06,399 --> 00:17:09,099
-[yelps]
-Is it cold, Mommy?

375
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:11,133
It's a little bit cold.

376
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:14,000
It always feels cold
when you first get in.

377
00:17:14,066 --> 00:17:16,533
If you keep moving, you'll warm up.

378
00:17:16,599 --> 00:17:18,500
Okay. I'll keep moving.

379
00:17:18,566 --> 00:17:21,033
[narrator] Mommy Pig has run
out of the sea.

380
00:17:21,099 --> 00:17:22,700
Let's get you dry.

381
00:17:22,766 --> 00:17:26,533
[narrator] Peppa, George and Daddy Pig
are warming Mommy Pig up

382
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:28,800
by rubbing her with towels.

383
00:17:29,033 --> 00:17:32,100
Ah, that's better.
Are you going for a swim, Daddy Pig?

384
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:34,066
Maybe not today.

385
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:37,533
-Who wants an ice cream?
-[children] Me!

386
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:40,433
[narrator] Everyone likes ice creams
at the seaside.

387
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:45,333
[snorts] I wanted to make sand castles.

388
00:17:45,399 --> 00:17:48,433
But the beach is covered in snow.

389
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:51,333
[snorts] We can make snow castles.

390
00:17:51,399 --> 00:17:52,500
[children] Ooh.

391
00:17:52,566 --> 00:17:55,133
First, we fill the buckets with snow.

392
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,500
[all giggling]

393
00:17:56,566 --> 00:18:00,133
We turn the buckets upside down,
give them a little tap,

394
00:18:00,666 --> 00:18:04,100
and, hey, presto, a snow castle!

395
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:06,633
[all] Snow castles!

396
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:08,800
I love the seaside.

397
00:18:09,033 --> 00:18:11,200
And I love the snow.

398
00:18:11,266 --> 00:18:14,766
I love the seaside and the snow.

399
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
[all laughing]

400
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,433
♪ We're all going on a seaside holiday ♪

401
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:26,300
♪ Sand castles, swimming and sunny skies ♪

402
00:18:26,366 --> 00:18:30,033
♪ We're all going on a seaside holiday ♪

403
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:33,633
♪ Sea and sand and ice cream, too ♪

